I am waiting for the `npm run check` command to complete. I will proceed with generating the final executor evidence report once it finishes.
I have fixed the issue where the `name` field in the frontmatter of plans retained Markdown escapes and single quotes, which caused invalid YAML when the title contained special characters.

Here is a summary of the changes:
1. **`src/exec-register.ts`**: Modified `registerPlanFrontmatter` to use `JSON.stringify(item.title)` instead of `escapeMarkdownInline(item.title).replace(/"/g, "'")` to safely encode the name field as a valid JSON/YAML string without escaping internal Markdown characters.
2. **`src/exec-plans.ts`**: Updated `frontmatter` to use `JSON.stringify(meta.name)` for general plan generation.
3. **`src/job.ts`**: Updated the scaffolded plan frontmatter to also use `JSON.stringify(definition.name)` instead of manual string replacement.
4. **`tests/src/exec-register-plan-escape.test.ts`**: 
   - Updated the existing assertion for the title in the frontmatter since the markdown escape was removed.
   - Added a new unit test to verify that titles containing special characters (`*`, `_`, `\`, `"`, `:`, `#`) are written into the plan's frontmatter such that they can be successfully parsed by `yaml.load` and perfectly match the original title.
5. **Formatting and Verification**: I ran `npx prettier --write` on all changed files and verified everything with `npm run check`. 

